    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0462" n="1196" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1196"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dupuy de Lôme to
                        Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-29"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your excellency’s polite note, under date of 27th instant, in
                    which you are pleased to inform me of the falsity of the rumors of the departure
                    of a filibustering expedition from St. Tammany Parish, La.</p>
                <p>In giving your excellency my most sincere thanks for the investigations made,</p>
                <p>I improve, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Dupuy de Lôme.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
